{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1012478-halt-and-catch-fire-with-a-shot-of-ascension","id":1012478,"title":"Halt and Catch Fire: With a shot of Ascension","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-05T03:54:52-08:00","id":1012478,"title":"Halt and Catch Fire: With a shot of Ascension","content":"Halt and Catch Fire is a TV show now on Netflix, I watched it, it's first season is pretty good and the second season isn't bad either.<br /> <br /> As I watched it, I kept getting the feeling that the shows main characters were players in the new era of war for the Digital Web that must have been raging in the 80's.<br /> <br /> The 80's was when personal computers and internet connections really became available in the home, all of a sudden a huge number of people were online for the first time and video games also entered the market in a big way. Ya, I know it was the 70's when video games and the internet were taking off but that was more in academic circles and it was the 80's when these things became widely accessible to consumers.<br /> <br /> By the 1980's, people were playing online games in the home and this era must have been one of renewed war between the Iterators and the VA's not to mention the rest of the Union and the other Technomancers.<br /> <br /> If you've watched the show, imagine Joe MacMillan as a rogue Syndicate agent or one who is on the fringe since leaving IBM.<br /> <br /> Cameron Howe is clearly a Virtual Adept with all the revolutionary beliefs and awkward social tendencies that brings.<br /> <br /> Gord and his wife are either Iterators who long to be free like the VA's or maybe Etherites.<br /> <br /> I love envisioning the show as a story of how a rogue Syndicate agent ends up finding himself while working on a project with a Virtual Adept and an Etherite/Iterator couple.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping someone else out there will share my interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T19:51:29-08:00","id":1012939,"title":"","content":"I really like Mackenzie Davis and I want to like this show, I'm just not that interested in the history of personal computing. ...Yet your take is interesting. In the context of Mage, all that stuff gains a new allure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T00:23:35-08:00","id":1013051,"title":"","content":"Indeed it does, the show made me think about the relationship between the syndicate and iteration x and how the two conventions were almost equally powerful in terms of driving the computer revolution. <br /> <br /> At the start of season one, Joe Macmillan is the epitome of the asshole syndicate boss who treats his 'employees' like they're expendable even though they have the ingenuity and he has the much more common talents of figuring people out and making them do what he wants (intuition and charisma).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Cameron is a classic VA who is on the fringe of society and can't handle being thrust into a successful position in mainstream computing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T07:15:08-08:00","id":1013141,"title":"","content":"I definitely agree that there are some nice parallels. Some of the themes, not to mention the actual historical progress shown in the series sort of make you want to run a prequel to the very first MtA materials set in the 90s. A prelude to the Digital Web, for instance. Doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}